        "firstName": "Glenda",
        "lastName": "COMAI",
        "role": "professor",
        "year": "",
        "linkedin": "https://www.linkedin.com/in/glenda-comai-152a956b/",
        "photo": "glenda-comai.jpg",
        "background": "Cell",
        "biosketch": "Prof. Glenda Comai is a CNRS permanent researcher at the Stem Cells and Development Unit of Institute Pasteur in Paris. Her current research bridges the developmental biology and stem cells fields with focus on craniofacial muscles. Using 3D-imaging, mouse genetics and single cell/single nuclear omics she seeks to understand how heterogeneity at the level of stem cells and myofibres is established, and how this impacts on muscular genetic disorders. She has a long-term interest in the mechanisms underlying tissue patterning during development."
      }
    ]
  },
